# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# cfg80211 kernel-config fragment for the Hi5622V100 clean-room Wi-Fi driver
# (wifi-cfg80211 lane, shared task task-104).
#
# The project 6.18.60 luofu kernel tree currently builds with
# "# CONFIG_CFG80211 is not set" (OpenWrt ships cfg80211 as the kmod-cfg80211
# package); a cfg80211 full-MAC driver can only work on a kernel that has it.
# This fragment is the handoff to the target/defconfig lane (task-107): add it
# to the hisilicon/luofu kernel config (target/linux/hisilicon/luofu/config-6.18)
# before the first bench attempt.
#
# CFG80211 selects CFG80211_HEADERS itself (net/wireless/Kconfig), which is
# what makes struct net_device's ieee80211_ptr field available to the
# out-of-tree build even on the current header-only tree.
#
# Wiring note for the target: if cfg80211 is built as a module, the driver
# module's modinfo already carries "depends=cfg80211" (modpost, via
# src/cfg80211-provider.symvers), so the OpenWrt package must depend on
# kmod-cfg80211 (or select CFG80211=y if the driver is built in).
CONFIG_WIRELESS=y
CONFIG_RFKILL=y
CONFIG_CFG80211=m
# CONFIG_CFG80211_HEADERS is selected by CONFIG_CFG80211 (bool, no prompt).
# MAC80211 is NOT needed: this driver is a cfg80211 full-MAC.
# CONFIG_CFG80211_CRDA_SUPPORT / CONFIG_CFG80211_USE_KERNEL_REGDB_KEYS keep
# their defaults (world regulatory domain from the kernel/regdb package); the
# vendor INI custom regdomain port is M6 (see REPORT.md sec 4/7).
